1
00:00:12,960 --> 00:00:16,550
I went over to Toru's place
for the first time yesterday.

2
00:00:16,550 --> 00:00:19,250
Ooooh! So how'd it go with him?!

3
00:00:19,250 --> 00:00:22,130
We didn't do anything like that, jeez.

4
00:00:22,130 --> 00:00:25,340
But he's got like, a massive
TV mounted to the wall,

5
00:00:25,340 --> 00:00:27,800
and loads of spare rooms on the
second <i>and</i> third floors of his house...

6
00:00:27,800 --> 00:00:29,590
I thought he was a poor plebian like me!

7
00:00:29,590 --> 00:00:31,460
S-Sorry to hear that...

8
00:00:31,460 --> 00:00:33,300
What's up?

9
00:00:33,300 --> 00:00:34,590
Shut it, you rich asshole!

10
00:00:34,590 --> 00:00:35,970
Wow, what the hell?

11
00:00:35,170 --> 00:00:36,710
You wanna order a cake?

12
00:00:36,710 --> 00:00:39,050
Yeah, I forgot to pre-order one this year.

13
00:00:39,050 --> 00:00:40,840
We should be able to handle it.

14
00:00:40,840 --> 00:00:45,460
We don't take that many pre-orders,
so we're not swamped or anything.

15
00:00:45,460 --> 00:00:47,250
What kind of cake do you want?

16
00:00:47,250 --> 00:00:50,000
Ooh, can I get one with
tons of whipped cream?

17
00:00:50,000 --> 00:00:51,340
Okay.

18
00:00:53,840 --> 00:00:56,550
I invited Yuna- <i>chan</i> over for Christmas!

19
00:00:56,550 --> 00:01:00,130
So we'll have you, Yuna- <i>chan</i> , Miyamura...

20
00:01:00,130 --> 00:01:02,380
Wait, is he gonna be able to come?

21
00:01:02,380 --> 00:01:06,130
You'd better invite him over.

22
00:01:06,130 --> 00:01:11,050
Hell, I don't care if you can't make it,
but Miyamura better be here.

23
00:01:11,050 --> 00:01:14,960
Sounds like you might be
sleeping in a manger on Christmas.

24
00:01:14,960 --> 00:01:17,090
Christmas?

25
00:01:17,090 --> 00:01:20,840
I'll probably be really busy helping
out at the shop from the 23rd on.

26
00:01:20,840 --> 00:01:22,590
Y-Yeah, I figured.

27
00:01:22,590 --> 00:01:26,380
Sorry. But if I get time,
I'll definitely come over!

28
00:01:26,380 --> 00:01:29,050
It's okay, you don't have
to squeeze in time for me.

29
00:01:29,050 --> 00:01:31,460
Once we eat dinner,
we're basically done anyway.

30
00:01:31,460 --> 00:01:32,630
Sorry.

31
00:01:32,630 --> 00:01:35,500
What?! You're not coming
for Christmas, Miyamura- <i>kun</i> ?!

32
00:01:35,500 --> 00:01:39,170
No, sorry. I already have lots of work
waiting for me at home today.

33
00:01:39,170 --> 00:01:43,210
You're not coming for Christmas?!
Please come! Please!

34
00:01:43,210 --> 00:01:45,300
S-Sorry, Sota...

35
00:01:45,300 --> 00:01:46,380
Please!

36
00:01:46,380 --> 00:01:47,210
I'm so sorry!

37
00:01:47,210 --> 00:01:48,460
Bro!

38
00:01:48,460 --> 00:01:50,000
Miyamura- <i>kun</i> !

39
00:01:50,000 --> 00:01:51,920
Please, bro!

40
00:01:51,920 --> 00:01:53,670
You know he's dating <i>me</i> , right?

41
00:01:53,670 --> 00:01:55,090
Miyamura- <i>kun</i> !

42
00:01:55,090 --> 00:01:57,800
Bro!

43
00:02:09,600 --> 00:02:21,780
Horimiya

44
00:03:30,750 --> 00:03:35,630
You know how up until recently,
I had a crush on Hori?

45
00:03:35,630 --> 00:03:36,960
How recently?

46
00:03:36,960 --> 00:03:39,920
I thought he gave up on her ages ago.

47
00:03:39,920 --> 00:03:42,960
And you know how there was
the whole thing with Kono- <i>san</i> ?

48
00:03:42,960 --> 00:03:45,000
Why does he think "we know" this?

49
00:03:45,000 --> 00:03:48,300
I have no idea what that
"whole thing" even was.

50
00:03:48,300 --> 00:03:51,380
And Yoshikawa and I are
definitely more than just friends,

51
00:03:51,380 --> 00:03:53,880
but I'm not gonna start
dating her or anything.

52
00:03:53,880 --> 00:04:01,420
What?

53
00:04:01,420 --> 00:04:03,710
I thought they were already dating.

54
00:04:03,710 --> 00:04:06,460
See, I thought that's how you'd react!

55
00:04:06,460 --> 00:04:11,500
I thought you thought
"I thought they were already dating"!

56
00:04:11,500 --> 00:04:14,340
Stop <i>thinking</i> , you're gonna
give Iura- <i>kun</i> an aneurism!

57
00:04:14,340 --> 00:04:16,130
You thought... we thought...

58
00:04:16,130 --> 00:04:18,340
Look, we're not dating!

59
00:04:18,340 --> 00:04:21,050
Well, okay, but...
don't you have a crush on her?

60
00:04:21,050 --> 00:04:22,670
Hell yeah, I like her!

61
00:04:22,670 --> 00:04:26,300
How are you not embarrassed
to admit that out loud?

62
00:04:26,300 --> 00:04:29,590
I mean, do you guys think this is weird?

63
00:04:29,590 --> 00:04:32,960
I don't think it's weird,
I'm just surprised.

64
00:04:32,960 --> 00:04:37,300
But, like, shouldn't you be more
concerned about what <i>she</i> thinks of you,

65
00:04:37,300 --> 00:04:41,300
rather than what <i>we</i> think of you?

66
00:04:41,300 --> 00:04:46,880
If you two are happy with your
current relationship, then that's fine.

67
00:04:46,880 --> 00:04:50,500
It's not my place to say
whether it's right or not.

68
00:04:50,500 --> 00:04:52,170
Wait, what?

69
00:04:52,170 --> 00:04:54,050
You're so cool, Sengoku- <i>san</i> !

70
00:04:54,050 --> 00:04:57,710
Advice sure sounds different when
it's coming from a master romancer.

71
00:04:57,710 --> 00:05:00,420
When was I ever a "master romancer"?!

72
00:05:05,670 --> 00:05:08,380
Hey, there you are, Toru!

73
00:05:08,200 --> 00:05:14,000
Hitherto, and Forevermore

74
00:05:08,380 --> 00:05:10,800
Can I come by your place
to play video games today?

75
00:05:10,800 --> 00:05:13,130
I wanna finish the game we started before.

76
00:05:13,130 --> 00:05:18,090
You do? Yeah, sure, you can come over.

77
00:05:18,090 --> 00:05:20,210
Wait, no, not today.

78
00:05:20,210 --> 00:05:22,210
Oh, why? You have plans already?

79
00:05:22,210 --> 00:05:25,300
No, I don't have plans.

80
00:05:25,300 --> 00:05:28,500
It's something else...

81
00:05:28,500 --> 00:05:30,960
No, it's fine. You can come over.

82
00:05:30,960 --> 00:05:34,000
Really? It's fine if
today's not a good day!

83
00:05:34,000 --> 00:05:37,800
No, it's fine. It was gonna
happen sooner or later...

84
00:05:39,420 --> 00:05:42,710
Sheesh, I never get used
to how huge your house is.

85
00:05:44,340 --> 00:05:46,380
I'm home.

86
00:05:46,380 --> 00:05:47,920
Why are you being so quiet?

87
00:05:47,920 --> 00:05:52,250
C'mon, Yoshikawa,
let's get upstairs. C'mon, c'mon!

88
00:05:52,250 --> 00:05:54,130
Huh?

89
00:05:54,130 --> 00:05:57,090
C'mon, c'moooon!

90
00:05:57,090 --> 00:05:59,880
Ugh, why is this hallway so long?!

91
00:05:59,880 --> 00:06:04,670
Oh, maybe his mom or dad are home...

92
00:06:04,670 --> 00:06:07,500
And he doesn't want me to meet them?

93
00:06:07,500 --> 00:06:10,630
Sorry to rush you, Yoshikawa.

94
00:06:10,630 --> 00:06:14,250
No, it's my fault.
I wish I were a hot guy.

95
00:06:14,250 --> 00:06:19,250
What? Wait, why?!
What are you talking about?

96
00:06:19,250 --> 00:06:21,880
I mean, if I were, you wouldn't...

97
00:06:21,880 --> 00:06:24,460
W-Wait, why are you locking the door?

98
00:06:24,460 --> 00:06:27,340
Huh? I mean...

99
00:06:27,340 --> 00:06:29,670
Wh-Why are you loosening your tie?!

100
00:06:29,670 --> 00:06:30,880
Huh?!

101
00:06:30,880 --> 00:06:34,380
I mean, I always take
my tie off when I get home.

102
00:06:36,800 --> 00:06:38,420
Yoshikawa--

103
00:06:43,710 --> 00:06:45,000
There.

104
00:06:46,000 --> 00:06:47,130
Huh?

105
00:06:47,130 --> 00:06:50,210
I'm not gonna try anything weird with you,

106
00:06:50,210 --> 00:06:54,210
but I don't want you to
be uncomfortable in here.

107
00:06:55,670 --> 00:06:58,750
I have no idea what I did wrong.

108
00:06:58,750 --> 00:07:01,340
I-It's not your fault!

109
00:07:01,340 --> 00:07:06,210
I'm not uncomfortable
or scared or anything.

110
00:07:06,210 --> 00:07:09,300
Oh, uh, is that right?

111
00:07:09,300 --> 00:07:11,130
Yeah.

112
00:07:11,130 --> 00:07:13,460
Oh.

113
00:07:16,050 --> 00:07:17,590
Toru- <i>kun</i> ?

114
00:07:17,590 --> 00:07:19,590
Oh, no, I forgot!

115
00:07:19,590 --> 00:07:20,380
Huh?

116
00:07:20,380 --> 00:07:23,800
That's weird. Why are you
closing the door on me?

117
00:07:23,800 --> 00:07:24,750
Do you have a friend over?

118
00:07:24,750 --> 00:07:29,750
Hey! Yeah, I do! Don't barge in!

119
00:07:29,750 --> 00:07:33,250
Wait, is that your mom? Is she your mom?!

120
00:07:33,250 --> 00:07:36,340
Oh, then let me get you two some drinks!

121
00:07:36,340 --> 00:07:38,840
No thanks! We're good! Thank you!

122
00:07:38,840 --> 00:07:40,750
She's blocking it with her foot.

123
00:07:40,750 --> 00:07:43,550
Come now, don't be rude to your guest!

124
00:07:43,550 --> 00:07:47,500
I can leave if I shouldn't be here, Toru!

125
00:07:47,500 --> 00:07:50,000
No, you're good!
Stay right there, Yoshikawa!

126
00:07:50,000 --> 00:07:52,000
Okay!

127
00:07:52,000 --> 00:07:55,340
So her name's Yoshikawa- <i>san</i> , then?

128
00:07:55,340 --> 00:07:57,130
Do you like cake?

129
00:07:57,130 --> 00:07:58,840
Y-Yes, ma'am.

130
00:07:58,840 --> 00:08:00,340
Let me go get you some.

131
00:08:00,340 --> 00:08:02,550
I told you, we're good!

132
00:08:02,550 --> 00:08:05,500
But she's our guest!

133
00:08:02,710 --> 00:08:04,210
Wh-Who is she?

134
00:08:04,210 --> 00:08:07,880
And holy crap, she's tall!

135
00:08:05,130 --> 00:08:07,630
Yashiro: 176 cm

136
00:08:05,130 --> 00:08:07,630
Ishikawa: 174 cm

137
00:08:07,880 --> 00:08:10,050
I'll go get that for you.

138
00:08:10,050 --> 00:08:11,460
Fine.

139
00:08:11,460 --> 00:08:14,380
And don't barge in without knocking.

140
00:08:15,380 --> 00:08:18,300
Weren't you gonna go get us some cake?!

141
00:08:18,300 --> 00:08:21,500
Okay, okay. You're so impatient.

142
00:08:23,840 --> 00:08:25,880
Is that your mom?

143
00:08:25,880 --> 00:08:31,210
Thank God she's not. That's Yashiro- <i>san</i> .
She helps out around the house.

144
00:08:31,210 --> 00:08:34,590
She always bombards me
with questions about you.

145
00:08:34,590 --> 00:08:35,170
Really?

146
00:08:35,170 --> 00:08:38,300
Like, "Who were you walking
with the other day?"

147
00:08:38,300 --> 00:08:41,630
"Who's that girl you're
always inviting over?"

148
00:08:41,630 --> 00:08:43,380
She's such a weirdo.

149
00:08:43,380 --> 00:08:46,000
Who, me?

150
00:08:46,000 --> 00:08:48,710
I told you to knock!

151
00:08:48,710 --> 00:08:50,710
Oh, c'mon.

152
00:08:50,710 --> 00:08:54,420
Which would you like,
shortcake or cheesecake?

153
00:08:54,420 --> 00:08:57,750
Short... no, cheesecake.

154
00:08:59,460 --> 00:09:03,670
Toru- <i>kun</i> , try anything funny,
and I'll tell your mother.

155
00:09:03,670 --> 00:09:07,340
I'm not gonna <i>try</i> anything now
that I know <i>you're</i> here, Yashiro- <i>san</i> !

156
00:09:07,340 --> 00:09:09,380
Holler if you need anything!

157
00:09:09,380 --> 00:09:11,420
Yeah, yeah.

158
00:09:11,420 --> 00:09:13,550
S-Sorry.

159
00:09:13,550 --> 00:09:17,500
She's all excited 'cause
I brought a girl over.

160
00:09:17,500 --> 00:09:18,960
She's nice, I swear.

161
00:09:18,960 --> 00:09:20,420
Oh, okay.

162
00:09:20,420 --> 00:09:25,840
I'm not gonna <i>try</i> anything now
that I know <i>you're</i> here, Yashiro- <i>san</i> !

163
00:09:25,710 --> 00:09:30,210
spin spin spin

164
00:09:25,840 --> 00:09:29,750
S-So if she <i>wasn't</i> here,
he <i>would</i> have t-t-t-t--

165
00:09:29,750 --> 00:09:31,500
Yoshikawa?

166
00:09:31,500 --> 00:09:34,500
Wait, what?! Something's
setting you off again!

167
00:09:34,500 --> 00:09:35,550
What's up?

168
00:09:35,550 --> 00:09:38,050
N-Nothing's up!

169
00:09:39,300 --> 00:09:42,710
What?! Don't just stare at me!

170
00:09:50,980 --> 00:09:52,480
rub rub rub

171
00:09:54,300 --> 00:09:56,670
You're here to play video games, right?

172
00:09:59,800 --> 00:10:01,960
Yeah!

173
00:10:01,960 --> 00:10:04,500
I'm gonna beat it today!

174
00:10:04,500 --> 00:10:07,500
Get it plugged in, Toru!

175
00:10:07,500 --> 00:10:11,630
I'm happy with the way things are.

176
00:10:13,880 --> 00:10:18,550
The cakes from this bakery
are great! Please, dig in!

